## Brief Overview

---

Malaga is an established destination for meetings: a report prepared for the Malaga Convention Bureau counted 2,190 meetings in the city in 2024, with 323,100 attendees. Malaga Event Gear supplies the audiovisual side of a MICE event: the [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) and the [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/), a technician who operates the sound and the microphones, and optional extras such as a lectern and modular stage platforms. Interpretation equipment, group hotels and anything outside our own inventory go through partners and suppliers.

## Key Highlights

---

-   2,190 meetings and 323,100 attendees in the city of Malaga in 2024, according to a report prepared for the Malaga Convention Bureau.
-   Corporate conventions and professional events were more than 80% of those meetings. Congresses were 9.3% and incentives 8.2%.
-   Our own inventory covers sound, a display or a projector, microphones and a technician. The MICE Pack is 490 euros ex VAT for up to 120 guests.
-   Simultaneous interpretation and voting systems are not in our own inventory. We coordinate them with a subcontracted partner.
-   We are not a venue, a DMC or an event agency, and we do not organize team building.

-   **Who delivers it?** Our crew delivers, installs and tests the equipment. We work delivery only, with no self pickup.
-   **How much notice?** At least 24 hours, and as early as your dates are set for a congress.
-   **What is not covered?** The venue, catering, registration, accommodation and any equipment outside our own inventory.

## Why Malaga Works for MICE Events

The size of the market is the first thing to check. A report prepared for the [Malaga Convention Bureau](https://sto.malaga.eu/export/sites/sto-malaga/.galleries/Documentos-Memorias/MEMORIA-2024-MCB.pdf) counted 2,190 meetings in the city in 2024, with 323,100 attendees in total. Corporate conventions and professional events were more than 80% of them, congresses 9.3% and incentives 8.2%. The average congress had more than 300 delegates, and 69.7% of all attendees came from outside the province, so most delegates need travel and a hotel.

Access is the second check. Malaga airport closed 2025 with [26,760,549 passengers](https://www.aena.es/es/prensa/el-aeropuerto-de-malaga-costa-del-sol-cierra-un-ano-historico-con-mas-de---267-millones-de-pasajeros-y-cerca-de-187.000-operaciones.html), according to AENA. That figure counts every traveler and not only business ones, so read it as a sign of how reachable the destination is.

The weather is the third. The [AEMET climate normals](https://www.aemet.es/es/serviciosclimaticos/datosclimatologicos/valoresclimatologicos?l=6155A&k=and) for the Malaga airport station, for 1981 to 2010, list 2,905 hours of sunshine a year and mean temperatures of 12.1 degrees Celsius in January and 25.5 in July. They are old normals, so use them as an orientation and check the forecast for your dates.

## Main Venues for Meetings and Congresses

These are the venues organizers name most often. The capacities are the venues' own, so confirm them with the venue for your layout, because they change with the arrangement of the room.

-   **FYCMA, the Malaga trade fair and congress center.** Its [sustainability report](https://fycma.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Informe-de-Sostenibilidad-Fycma-2025.pdf) lists two exhibition pavilions with 19,500 square meters, an auditorium for up to 900 people and another for 600.
-   **Palacio de Congresos y Exposiciones de Torremolinos.** Its main room, the [Sala Torremolinos](https://palacio-congresos.es/?p=5305), holds 817 people in total, 491 with working tables and 326 without, and has booths for simultaneous interpretation into five languages.
-   **Palacio de Congresos de Marbella.** [Its own site](https://marbellacongresos.com/) lists an auditorium of 1,520 seats and 10,000 square meters of surface.
-   **Hotel convention centers on the Costa del Sol.** Many congresses and summits are held in the meeting rooms of a hotel. We worked at one in Torremolinos, described below.

We are not affiliated with any of these venues. We deliver to them like any other address in our service area.

## What the Venue Gives You and What You Bring

A venue's own equipment list is where to start. The Torremolinos palace, for example, lists its interpretation booths, and it is normal that a room has some sound and some screens of its own. Before you hire anything, ask the venue three things: which sound, screens and microphones are included, who operates them and what has to be brought from outside.

The second answer matters most. A room with equipment and nobody to run it leaves the speaker alone with a microphone, while a technician who knows the equipment solves a fault in the middle of a session. Whoever you choose, agree who calls whom if something fails, and give that person the schedule of the sessions.

