## What We Supply at a MICE Event

Our own inventory covers the common needs of a corporate meeting or a congress:

-   The [MICE Pack](/packages/mice/) at 490 euros ex VAT, for up to 120 guests: professional active speakers, a 60 inch LED display, one gooseneck plus one wireless handheld microphone and a technician on site for up to 6 hours. A lectern is an optional extra at 50 euros and modular stage platforms are 35 euros per square meter. An extra hour of the technician is 40 euros.
-   The [Basic MICE Pack](/packages/basic-mice/) at 295 euros ex VAT, for up to 40 guests: a projector with a screen, a sound system and one gooseneck microphone. The technician is optional at 240 euros per day.

The technician operates the sound and the microphones and solves a fault with the sound, the projector or the screen. The speaker runs their own slides. For a room or a guest list beyond what these packs cover, tell us the room and the program, and we check what we can supply from our own inventory and what we would source.

## Run of Show for Corporate Events

A run of show is the minute by minute list of what happens on stage, and the technician needs the audio side of it before the day. Send it with your booking as a short document with a time block for each session: start and end times, who speaks and which microphone they use.

Mark every change of microphone. The MICE Pack includes one gooseneck and one wireless handheld, so a lectern speaker followed by a host with the handheld tells the technician when to switch. If you need more microphones than the pack includes, give us the count and we check what we can supply from our own inventory.

The speaker runs their own slides, not our technician, so write down who advances them and how the handover between speakers works. Mark the breaks too, because a break is when the technician can run a sound check and the next speaker can test their microphone. Name who calls the cues, and agree what happens if the program runs long: the MICE Pack includes the technician for up to 6 hours, and an extra hour is 40 euros.

## What We Source With Partners

A MICE event often needs things we do not have, and this is how we handle them:

-   **Simultaneous interpretation and voting systems.** We do not own this equipment. We coordinate it with a subcontracted partner, so we do not promise a specific model or a price until we have checked.
-   **Group hotels.** Delegates from outside Malaga need somewhere to stay. For group bookings, our partner [Top Group Express](https://topgroupexpress.com/en) has years of experience reserving hotels for groups, working with the agencies, DMCs and companies that organize a delegation's travel. We handle the sound and the screens, they handle the rooms.
-   **Streaming, hybrid events and video walls.** These are not in our own inventory. Tell us what you need and we look for a solution with our suppliers, if there is one.

The rest of the event, such as the venue, the catering, registration and any team building activity, is for your organizer or agency. We are the audiovisual part of it.

